<title>CHINA: China textile industry shows signs of recovery.</title>
<headline>China textile industry shows signs of recovery.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's textile industry is showing signs of recovery with the number of loss-making enterprises falling to 56 percent of the total in the first five months of 1997, the Business News said on Friday.</p>
<p>That figure was down on the same year-ago period by four percentage points, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Total losses fell to 1.8 billion yuan ($216.9 million) in that period, down a year-on-year 600 million yuan, it said.</p>
<p>China's textile export turnover surged to $16 billion in the first five months of 1997, an increase of 33 percent compared with the same 1996 period, it said.</p>
<p>($1=8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>-- Shanghai newsroom (8621) 6279-7004</p>
</text>
